+### Why named entity references
+
+This shape reuses the existing identity normalization, primary-identity, ambiguity,
+auto-create, and trait semantics once per logical endpoint. Both event attributions and
+entity relationships can reuse the result, but resolving a relationship-only endpoint
+does not automatically add it to event attribution/visibility. That separation matters:
+attributions answer which entities the event is connected to for recall and ACL; a
+domain edge is a different fact. Inline endpoint selectors duplicate identity policy and
+can drift. Keying the current attribution array avoids duplication but still conflates
+those two meanings. A named resolver map is additive: existing inline attributions remain
+valid, while new connectors use `entityRefs`.
